## Lead's addendum (2026-11-16, second version)

Written by the lead after reading the round's return at 19:22 local time: the reconciler's output, the implementers'
summaries and the three skeptics' reports. Before 19:22 the lead had read no comparison statistic of this round. The
tallies below come from the final `mismatches.json` (18:49:50) and from A's and B's `results.json`; the skeptics'
files are in `V\skeptic\blindness`, `V\skeptic\numbers` and `V\skeptic\reconcile`, and the agents' returned reports,
byte for byte, in `V\_lead\returns\`. The lead's scripts are in `V\_lead\scripts\`: `recover_writes.py` (the
recovery of the reconciler's text), `tally.py` (A2), `scan_shap_mtimes.py` (the scan in A4) and `b1_tables.py` (A6).
The first version of this addendum (19:31) was read by two report checkers; this version answers their findings (A7).

### A1. Corrections to the reconciler's text

Opening and reading

1. Section 1, "None of the compare outputs was opened before 2026-11-16 18:24:54 in this round": true of the files
   that hold statistics (the AW3 and AW4 tables, `AW4_main_row.json`, the importance, families, pairs and
   bootstrap_stats parquet files, and the pairs done record), not of all ten. `per_lead.json` (its structural keys
   only) and `bootstrap_draws.npy` had been opened earlier in the round by the spec writer, A and B, as the brief
   allows (A's `work\opened_items_<p>.json` and `work\opened_b1.json`). The 50 logged openings are the reconciler's
   own first openings.
2. Section 1, "All other compare files of the current outputs had not been opened before": PROTOCOL.md section 14
   records that, apart from coral's `AW4_table.md`, only the current comparisons' logs and the structural fields of
   their `per_lead.json` (models, main set, declined list, links, rows, sample hash) were read before this round
   (lines 829-831 and 936-938), and that text searches on 2026-11-14 and 2026-11-15 passed over the AW3 and AW4
   tables without showing a line (lines 941-946).
